.he "vi (1)                       8/12/26                       vi (1)"
.fo "                               -#-"
.in 5
.rm 65
.bd
NAME
.in +5
.br
.bd
vi
- a screen editor
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
SYNTAX
.in +5
.br
.bd
vi [ -d ] file
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
DESCRIPTION
.in +5
.br
Vi is STevie, Tim Thompson's editor for vi enthusiasts, ported here.
It takes one file, which it reads into memory; a file that does not
exist yet is not an error and is announced as a new one.
.sp
The commands are vi's, in the subset STevie implements: the addresses
and the operators, the insert commands, the yank buffer, marks and
searches.  Colon takes a command line.
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
OPTIONS
.in +5
.br
.in +10
.ti -10
-d	Set the debugging flag.

.in -10
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
COLON COMMANDS
.in +5
.br
.nf
     :w       write
     :q :q!   quit, and quit without writing
     :wq      write and quit
     :e :e!   edit another file
     :r       read a file in after this line
     :.r      read a file in at this line
     :f       the file name and where you are
     :.=      the current line number
     :$=      the number of lines
     :set     set an option; tabstop is the one
.fi
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
NOTES
.in +5
.br
The sizes are tuned to fill a sixty-four kilobyte machine: a file of
up to sixteen thousand characters, a screen of up to sixty lines of
eighty columns.  A terminal of fewer than three lines or sixteen
columns is refused.
.sp
The debugging flag sets a variable that nothing reads, so it does
nothing at present.
.sp
The usage message calls the program stevie, which is the name it was
ported under.
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
SEE ALSO
.in +5
.br
s (1)
